<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs of main results</h2>

<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4 (Sufficiency). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given any <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying Assumption <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 2.2. ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, the existence of <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is proved by the following construction:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})={\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})+(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})={\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})+(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">The proof will be done by choosing a function <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon:{\mathbb{X}}\to{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon:{\mathbb{X}}\to{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Functions <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> are both globally Lipschitz continuous on <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">The existence of such a <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> function is deferred to Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. Now, let’s suppose such a <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is given and finish the whole proof. First, let’s check the contractivity of <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.E11" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) as <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed. For any <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})-{\mathcal{G}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{x}})=(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}))-(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))(\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}))=(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))({\bm{y}}-\hat{{\bm{y}}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})-{\mathcal{G}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}},{\bm{x}})=(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}))-(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))(\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}))=(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))({\bm{y}}-\hat{{\bm{y}}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is contractive for <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, the continuity of the contraction modulus <math id="A1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))</annotation></semantics></math> is a direct result of the continuity of <math id="A1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, we check the Lipschitz continuity as <math id="A1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed. For any <math id="A1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}},\hat{{\bm{x}}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}},\hat{{\bm{x}}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{x}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{x}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big({\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}\Big)-\Big({\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{x}}})-{\bm{y}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big({\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}\Big)-\Big({\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{x}}})-{\bm{y}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big({\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}+(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}))\Big)-\Big({\mathcal{F}}(\hat{{\bm{x}}})-{\bm{y}}+(1-\varepsilon(\hat{{\bm{x}}}))({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}(\hat{{\bm{x}}}))\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big({\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}+(1-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}))({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}))\Big)-\Big({\mathcal{F}}(\hat{{\bm{x}}})-{\bm{y}}+(1-\varepsilon(\hat{{\bm{x}}}))({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}(\hat{{\bm{x}}}))\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\varepsilon({\bm{x}})({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}))+\varepsilon(\hat{{\bm{x}}})({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}(\hat{{\bm{x}}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\varepsilon({\bm{x}})({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}))+\varepsilon(\hat{{\bm{x}}})({\bm{y}}-{\mathcal{F}}(\hat{{\bm{x}}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big(-\varepsilon({\bm{x}})+\varepsilon(\hat{{\bm{x}}})\Big){\bm{y}}+\Big(\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})-\varepsilon(\hat{{\bm{x}}}){\mathcal{F}}(\hat{{\bm{x}}})\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big(-\varepsilon({\bm{x}})+\varepsilon(\hat{{\bm{x}}})\Big){\bm{y}}+\Big(\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})-\varepsilon(\hat{{\bm{x}}}){\mathcal{F}}(\hat{{\bm{x}}})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">With a fixed <math id="A1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from the Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, by denoting the Lipschitz constants of <math id="A1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{x}}})\|\leq L_{\varepsilon}\|{\bm{x}}-\hat{{\bm{x}}}\|\cdot\|{\bm{y}}\|+L_{\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}}\|{\bm{x}}-\hat{{\bm{x}}}\|\leq\Big(L_{\varepsilon}\|{\bm{y}}\|+L_{\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}}\Big)\|{\bm{x}}-\hat{{\bm{x}}}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\hat{{\bm{x}}})\|\leq L_{\varepsilon}\|{\bm{x}}-\hat{{\bm{x}}}\|\cdot\|{\bm{y}}\|+L_{\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}}\|{\bm{x}}-\hat{{\bm{x}}}\|\leq\Big(L_{\varepsilon}\|{\bm{y}}\|+L_{\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}}\Big)\|{\bm{x}}-\hat{{\bm{x}}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the Lipschitz constant of <math id="A1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L:=L_{\varepsilon}\|{\bm{y}}\|+L_{\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L:=L_{\varepsilon}\|{\bm{y}}\|+L_{\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, grows linearly w.r.t. <math id="A1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, which finishes the whole proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Below we provide the core theorem used in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4 (Sufficiency). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a> and its proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying Assumption <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 2.2. ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, there exists a function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon:{\mathbb{X}}\to{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon:{\mathbb{X}}\to{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> are both globally Lipschitz continuous on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the closure of set <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this proof, we will first extend <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, construct the <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> function on <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and finally prove the global Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Extension to <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> First we extend <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> by the limit relative to <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}(\bar{\bm{x}})=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}\to\bar{\bm{x}}}{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}),\quad&amp;&amp;\textup{if $\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}\to\bar{\bm{x}}}{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})$ exists},\\
&amp;0,&amp;&amp;\textup{otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>∋</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>∋</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mtext> exists</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}(\bar{\bm{x}})=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}\to\bar{\bm{x}}}{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}),\quad&amp;&amp;\textup{if $\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}\to\bar{\bm{x}}}{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})$ exists},\\
&amp;0,&amp;&amp;\textup{otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that even if <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuously extendable to <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is still possible that <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not locally Lipschitz continuous at the point <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A simple example is the function <math id="A1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is continuous as <math id="A1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and locally Lipschitz continuous for all points <math id="A1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> but NOT locally Lipschitz at <math id="A1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We collect all these points (where <math id="A1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not locally Lipschitz) into the set <math id="A1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}}):=\left\{{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}:\textup{${\mathcal{F}}$ is not locally Lipschitz continuous at ${\bm{x}}$}\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext> is not locally Lipschitz continuous at </mtext><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}}):=\left\{{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}:\textup{${\mathcal{F}}$ is not locally Lipschitz continuous at ${\bm{x}}$}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">For brevity, we will use <math id="A1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote <math id="A1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})</annotation></semantics></math>. It holds that <math id="A1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a closed set (ref. to Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>) and <math id="A1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Constructing a function <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon:\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\to{\mathbb{R}}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon:\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\to{\mathbb{R}}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">Now let’s define a set including all points that are very “safe”, i.e., sufficiently far from the discontinuity set <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, given a positive real number <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="A1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is define by</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}:=\big\{{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}:d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})\geq r\big\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}:=\big\{{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}:d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})\geq r\big\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})</annotation></semantics></math> means the distance of <math id="A1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the closedness of <math id="A1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> can be derived from the continuity of the distance function. Since <math id="A1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact, <math id="A1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> must be compact. Note that <math id="A1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> are disjoint, hence <math id="A1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz continuous everywhere on <math id="A1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thanks to the fact that local Lipschitz continuity on a compact set implies global Lipschitz continuity (ref to Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>), we can conclude that <math id="A1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded and globally Lipschitz continuous on <math id="A1.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the following two supremums exist, as long as the cardinality (number of elements) of <math id="A1.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle h_{1}(r)=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r},{\bm{x}}_{1}\not={\bm{x}}_{2}}\frac{\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|}{\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|},\quad&amp;&amp;\mathrm{card}({\mathbb{D}}_{r})\geq 2,\\
&amp;0,&amp;&amp;\textup{otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>card</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{1}(r)=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r},{\bm{x}}_{1}\not={\bm{x}}_{2}}\frac{\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|}{\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|},\quad&amp;&amp;\mathrm{card}({\mathbb{D}}_{r})\geq 2,\\
&amp;0,&amp;&amp;\textup{otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle h_{2}(r)=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\sup_{{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}}\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})\|,\quad&amp;&amp;\mathrm{card}({\mathbb{D}}_{r})\geq 1,\\
&amp;0,&amp;&amp;\textup{otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>card</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{2}(r)=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\sup_{{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}}\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})\|,\quad&amp;&amp;\mathrm{card}({\mathbb{D}}_{r})\geq 1,\\
&amp;0,&amp;&amp;\textup{otherwise}.\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Here, both <math id="A1.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are non-negative and monotone non-increasing on <math id="A1.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,+\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,+\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we define:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{h}(r)=\frac{1}{h_{1}(r)+h_{2}(r)+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{h}(r)=\frac{1}{h_{1}(r)+h_{2}(r)+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">It has the following properties:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:5mm;">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Bounded: <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\hat{h}(r)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\hat{h}(r)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Monotone : <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{h}(r_{1})\leq\hat{h}(r_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{h}(r_{1})\leq\hat{h}(r_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;r_{1}\leq r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;r_{1}\leq r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. (Due to the monotonicity of <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Naturally extended to <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{r\to 0_{+}}\hat{h}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{r\to 0_{+}}\hat{h}(r)</annotation></semantics></math> exists. (Due to the monotonicity of <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{h}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{h}(r)h_{i}(r)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{h}(r)h_{i}(r)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">These properties implies that <math id="A1.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is Riemann integrable on <math id="A1.p5.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,+\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,+\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we can define the following function:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\varepsilon}(r):=\int_{0}^{r}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\varepsilon}(r):=\int_{0}^{r}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">with the following properties:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:5mm;">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\varepsilon}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\varepsilon}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Monotone increasing. This is a straightforward result of the fact that <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{h}(s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{h}(s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Strictly positive as <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This is also straightforward as <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{h}(s)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{h}(s)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz continuous on <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[0,+\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,+\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq r_{1}\leq r_{2}&lt;+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq r_{1}\leq r_{2}&lt;+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\varepsilon}(r_{1})-\hat{\varepsilon}(r_{2})|=\hat{\varepsilon}(r_{2})-\hat{\varepsilon}(r_{1})=\int_{r_{1}}^{r_{2}}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s\leq\left(\sup_{r\geq 0}\hat{h}(r)\right)|r_{1}-r_{2}|=|r_{1}-r_{2}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\varepsilon}(r_{1})-\hat{\varepsilon}(r_{2})|=\hat{\varepsilon}(r_{2})-\hat{\varepsilon}(r_{1})=\int_{r_{1}}^{r_{2}}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s\leq\left(\sup_{r\geq 0}\hat{h}(r)\right)|r_{1}-r_{2}|=|r_{1}-r_{2}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">With such a <math id="A1.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\varepsilon}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\varepsilon}(r)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can define <math id="A1.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})=\frac{\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}{1+\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})=\frac{\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}{1+\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">It holds that <math id="A1.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.p5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.p5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A1.p5.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.p5.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon({\bm{x}})&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.p5.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Establishing Lipschitz continuity.<span id="A1.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Since the distance function <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz continuous <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, Theorem 4.8 (1)]</cite>, the Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> implies the Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, for all <math id="A1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})\Big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})\Big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\frac{\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}{1+\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}-\frac{\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}{1+\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\frac{\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}{1+\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}-\frac{\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}{1+\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\textup{$\frac{x}{1+x}$ is 1-Lipschitz as $\left(\frac{x}{1+x}\right)^{\prime}=\frac{1}{(1+x)^{2}}$}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mtext> is 1-Lipschitz as </mtext><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\textup{$\frac{x}{1+x}$ is 1-Lipschitz as $\left(\frac{x}{1+x}\right)^{\prime}=\frac{1}{(1+x)^{2}}$}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)-\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)-\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\textup{Lipschitz continuity of $\hat{\varepsilon}$})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Lipschitz continuity of </mtext><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\textup{Lipschitz continuity of $\hat{\varepsilon}$})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big|d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})-d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big|\leq\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big|d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})-d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big|\leq\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\textup{Lipschitz continuity of $d$})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Lipschitz continuity of </mtext><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\textup{Lipschitz continuity of $d$})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, to complete the whole proof, it’s enough to show the global Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact, and thanks to Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, it’s enough to show <math id="A1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz everywhere on <math id="A1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">First, we consider local Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Due to Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, <math id="A1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> must be open relative to <math id="A1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there must be a small enough <math id="A1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{U}}:={\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r)\cap\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕌</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{U}}:={\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r)\cap\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Pick <math id="A1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕌</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E12X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E12Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})+\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})+\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E12Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})\big\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\big\|+|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})|\cdot\big\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\big\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})\big\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\big\|+|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})|\cdot\big\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\big\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since both <math id="A1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> are locally Lipschitz and locally bounded everywhere on <math id="A1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, they must be Lipschitz and bounded within <math id="A1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the local Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> immediately follows from (<a href="#A1.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>). Note that <math id="A1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrarily picked from <math id="A1.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A1.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz everywhere on <math id="A1.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we consider local Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider its neighborhood <math id="A1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{U}}:={\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},1)\cap\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕌</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{U}}:={\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},1)\cap\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and pick <math id="A1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕌</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we need to consider three cases. The first case is both <math id="A1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> belong to the discontinuity set <math id="A1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, it holds that <math id="A1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})=\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})=\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and hence</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\Big\|=0\leq\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\Big\|=0\leq\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">The second case is that one of the point is in <math id="A1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> while the other is not, we suppose <math id="A1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1}\in{\mathbb{D}},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1}\in{\mathbb{D}},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\Big\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\Big\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\Big\|\leq\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\Big\|\leq\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\int_{0}^{d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s\right)\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\int_{0}^{d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s\right)\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{h}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{h}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\textup{Monotonicity of $\hat{h}$})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Monotonicity of </mtext><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\textup{Monotonicity of $\hat{h}$})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{h}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{h}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\textup{Definition of $h_{2}$})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Definition of </mtext><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\textup{Definition of $h_{2}$})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\hat{h}(r)\cdot h_{2}(r)&lt;1\textup{ as }r\geq 0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\hat{h}(r)\cdot h_{2}(r)&lt;1\textup{ as }r\geq 0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})-d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\leq\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})-d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\leq\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we consider the last case where <math id="A1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, we assume</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\leq d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\leq d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then the definition of <math id="A1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> implies that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex41X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\Big(h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})),h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))\Big)\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\Big(h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})),h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))\Big)\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, applying (<a href="#A1.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) and the above inequalities, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})\big\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\big\|+|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})|\cdot\big\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\big\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})\big\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\big\|+|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})|\cdot\big\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\big\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})\cdot h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})|\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})\cdot h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2})|\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)\cdot h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+\left|\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)-\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)\right|\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)\cdot h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+\left|\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)-\hat{\varepsilon}\Big(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big)\right|\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\int_{0}^{d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s\right)\cdot h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+\left(\int_{d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})}^{d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s\right)\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\int_{0}^{d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s\right)\cdot h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+\left(\int_{d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})}^{d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})}\hat{h}(s)\mathrm{d}s\right)\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot\hat{h}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot\hat{h}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot h_{1}(d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\Big|d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})-d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big|\cdot\hat{h}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\Big|d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})-d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big|\cdot\hat{h}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))\cdot h_{2}(d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+\Big|d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})-d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+\Big|d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})-d({\bm{x}}_{2},{\mathbb{D}})\Big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d({\bm{x}}_{1},{\mathbb{D}})\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|+\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">The last inequality results from <math id="A1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{h}(r)\cdot(h_{1}(r)+h_{2}(r))&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>h</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{h}(r)\cdot(h_{1}(r)+h_{2}(r))&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. And the above inequalities imply</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq(\textup{diam}(\overline{{\mathbb{X}}})+1)\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>diam</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{1}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{1})-\varepsilon({\bm{x}}_{2}){\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq(\textup{diam}(\overline{{\mathbb{X}}})+1)\cdot\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.8.1" class="ltx_text">Combining all the results together, we have <math id="A1.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally <math id="A1.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textup{diam}(\overline{{\mathbb{X}}})+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>diam</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textup{diam}(\overline{{\mathbb{X}}})+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz at any <math id="A1.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the compactness of <math id="A1.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> concludes the global Lipschitz continuous of <math id="A1.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which finishes the whole proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Follows are some lemmas (as well as their proofs) that we used in the proof of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be closed and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}:{\mathbb{T}}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}:{\mathbb{T}}\to{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote by <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})\subset{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝕋</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})\subset{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of points at which <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">not</em>
locally Lipschitz. Then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> is closed (in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz (relative to <math id="A1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>) at <math id="A1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕋</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> if there exist <math id="A1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{u}})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{v}})\|\leq L\,\|{\bm{u}}-{\bm{v}}\|\qquad\text{for all }{\bm{u}},{\bm{v}}\in{\mathbb{T}}\cap{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{u}})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{v}})\|\leq L\,\|{\bm{u}}-{\bm{v}}\|\qquad\text{for all }{\bm{u}},{\bm{v}}\in{\mathbb{T}}\cap{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{G}}:={\mathbb{T}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔾</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{G}}:={\mathbb{T}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of points where <math id="A1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A1.p10.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">is</em> locally Lipschitz.
We first show that <math id="A1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is relatively open in <math id="A1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="A1.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and choose <math id="A1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,L</annotation></semantics></math> as above.
If <math id="A1.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}^{\prime}\in{\mathbb{T}}\cap{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}^{\prime}\in{\mathbb{T}}\cap{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}}^{\prime},r/2)\subset{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}}^{\prime},r/2)\subset{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r)</annotation></semantics></math>; hence the same <math id="A1.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> works on
<math id="A1.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}\cap{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}}^{\prime},r/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}\cap{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}}^{\prime},r/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz at <math id="A1.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore
<math id="A1.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}\cap{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r/2)\subset{\mathbb{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝔾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}\cap{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{x}},r/2)\subset{\mathbb{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving that <math id="A1.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is open in <math id="A1.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, <math id="A1.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})={\mathbb{T}}\setminus{\mathbb{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝕋</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔾</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})={\mathbb{T}}\setminus{\mathbb{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is closed in <math id="A1.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> is closed in <math id="A1.p10.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, every set closed in <math id="A1.p10.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> is also closed in <math id="A1.p10.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence <math id="A1.p10.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}({\mathcal{F}})</annotation></semantics></math> is closed in <math id="A1.p10.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> as well.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a compact set. If <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz everywhere on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then it must be globally Lipschitz on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume, to the contrary, that <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not globally Lipschitz on <math id="A1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we can choose sequences <math id="A1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{x}}_{k}\}_{k\geq 1},\{{\bm{y}}_{k}\}_{k\geq 1}\subset{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi>𝕋</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{x}}_{k}\}_{k\geq 1},\{{\bm{y}}_{k}\}_{k\geq 1}\subset{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{k})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{y}}_{k})\|}{\|{\bm{x}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k}\|}\xrightarrow{k\to\infty}\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{k})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{y}}_{k})\|}{\|{\bm{x}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k}\|}\xrightarrow{k\to\infty}\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Local Lipschitzness implies continuity of <math id="A1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so by compactness <math id="A1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded:
there exists <math id="A1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{z}})\|\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{z}})\|\leq C</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}\in{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕋</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}\in{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{k})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{y}}_{k})\|\leq 2C\qquad\text{for all }k," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{k})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{y}}_{k})\|\leq 2C\qquad\text{for all }k,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore (<a href="#A1.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) forces <math id="A1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{x}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k}\|\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{x}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k}\|\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">By sequential compactness of <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, passing to a subsequence (not relabeled) we may assume <math id="A1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{k}\to{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕋</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{k}\to{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>; since <math id="A1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{x}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k}\|\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{x}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k}\|\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have <math id="A1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{k}\to{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{k}\to{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz at <math id="A1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> large enough we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{k})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{y}}_{k})\|}{\|{\bm{x}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k}\|}\leq L," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\|{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}}_{k})-{\mathcal{F}}({\bm{y}}_{k})\|}{\|{\bm{x}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k}\|}\leq L,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">for some <math id="A1.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, which contradicts (<a href="#A1.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>). Therefore <math id="A1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> must be globally Lipschitz on <math id="A1.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Note that Lemmas <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma A.2. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> are standard in real analysis, we provide concise proofs of them for the sake of completeness. Next we provide proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 2.5 (Necessity). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 2.5 (Necessity). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the closure of <math id="A1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this proof, we will first extend the operator <math id="A1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\times\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\times\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then analyze its properties on this closed domain.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Extension to <math id="A1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.p15.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> For any <math id="A1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is globally Lipschitz continuous on <math id="A1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence its extension is naturally define by</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\bar{\bm{x}}):=\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}\to\bar{\bm{x}}}{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}}),\quad\textup{for all }\bar{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>∋</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\bar{\bm{x}}):=\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}\to\bar{\bm{x}}}{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}}),\quad\textup{for all }\bar{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">Different from the proof of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem A.1. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> where <math id="A1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> might be not locally Lipschitz at <math id="A1.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> even if it is continuous at <math id="A1.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, here the extended <math id="A1.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> must be Lipschitz at <math id="A1.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence Lipschitz on the overall set <math id="A1.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be verified by examining the difference quotient for <math id="A1.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]:=\frac{\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}}_{2})\|}{\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]:=\frac{\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}}_{2})\|}{\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>’s Lipschitz constant on <math id="A1.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A1.p15.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L({\bm{y}}):=\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{X}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L({\bm{y}}):=\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{X}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A1.p15.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p15.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}]=\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}_{2}\to\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]\leq\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{X}}:{\bm{x}}_{2}\neq{\bm{x}}_{1}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]\leq L({\bm{y}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>∋</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}]=\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}_{2}\to\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]\leq\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{X}}:{\bm{x}}_{2}\neq{\bm{x}}_{1}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]\leq L({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A1.p15.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1}\neq\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1}\neq\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}]=\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}_{1}\to\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1}}\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}_{2}\to\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]\leq\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{X}}:{\bm{x}}_{2}\neq{\bm{x}}_{1}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]=L({\bm{y}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>∋</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>∋</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}]=\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}_{1}\to\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1}}\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}_{2}\to\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]\leq\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{X}}:{\bm{x}}_{2}\neq{\bm{x}}_{1}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]=L({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p15.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we obtain an upper bound for <math id="A1.p15.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>’s Lipschitz constant on <math id="A1.p15.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\left(\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{X}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}],\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\in{\mathbb{X}},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}],\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\left(\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{X}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}],\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\in{\mathbb{X}},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};{\bm{x}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}],\sup_{{\bm{x}}_{1}\neq{\bm{x}}_{2}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}}\Delta{\mathcal{G}}[{\bm{y}};\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{1},\bar{{\bm{x}}}_{2}]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\left(L({\bm{y}}),L({\bm{y}}),L({\bm{y}})\right)=L({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\left(L({\bm{y}}),L({\bm{y}}),L({\bm{y}})\right)=L({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p15.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p15.6.1" class="ltx_text">That is, for any <math id="A1.p15.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p15.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is globally Lipschitz on <math id="A1.p15.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the Lipschitz constant is the same as that of <math id="A1.p15.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, let’s consider the Lipschitz constant (contraction modulus) w.r.t. <math id="A1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> when fixing <math id="A1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\bar{\bm{x}})=\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}\to\bar{\bm{x}}}\mu({\bm{x}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>∋</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\bar{\bm{x}})=\lim_{{\mathbb{X}}\ni{\bm{x}}\to\bar{\bm{x}}}\mu({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu({\bm{x}})&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu({\bm{x}})&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, by taking limit, we have <math id="A1.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\mu(\bar{\bm{x}})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\mu(\bar{\bm{x}})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. For those <math id="A1.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\bar{\bm{x}})&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\bar{\bm{x}})&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the operator <math id="A1.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,\bar{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,\bar{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is still contractive. But if <math id="A1.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\bar{\bm{x}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\bar{\bm{x}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the operator <math id="A1.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,\bar{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,\bar{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is not contractive.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Defining <math id="A1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.p17.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We collect all points <math id="A1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}</annotation></semantics></math> where the operator <math id="A1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is not contractive:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}:=\left\{{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}:\mu({\bm{x}})=1\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}:=\left\{{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}:\mu({\bm{x}})=1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">and define a “safe” set that is sufficiently far from <math id="A1.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}:=\big\{{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}:d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})\geq r\big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}:=\big\{{\bm{x}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}:d({\bm{x}},{\mathbb{D}})\geq r\big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A1.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}=\bigcup_{r&gt;0}{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}=\bigcup_{r&gt;0}{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕏</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}\subset\overline{{\mathbb{X}}}\setminus{\mathbb{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}\subset\bigcup_{r&gt;0}{\mathbb{D}}_{r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">⊂</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}\subset\bigcup_{r&gt;0}{\mathbb{D}}_{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p17.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.4.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A1.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we can obtain a uniform contraction modulus of the operator <math id="A1.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>: There is a constant <math id="A1.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{r}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{r}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{x}})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{2},{\bm{x}})\|\leq\mu_{r}\|{\bm{y}}_{1}-{\bm{y}}_{2}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{x}})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{2},{\bm{x}})\|\leq\mu_{r}\|{\bm{y}}_{1}-{\bm{y}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p17.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p17.5.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A1.p17.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p17.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, which follows immediately from the continuity of <math id="A1.p17.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and the compactness of <math id="A1.p17.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Banach fixed-point theorem, the operator <math id="A1.p17.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> must have a unique fixed point <math id="A1.p17.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A1.p17.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">To complete the proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 2.5 (Necessity). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>, thanks to the fact that <math id="A1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}\subset\bigcup_{r&gt;0}{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕏</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}\subset\bigcup_{r&gt;0}{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, it’s enough to show that: For any <math id="A1.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a constant <math id="A1.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq C_{r}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq C_{r}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">holds for all <math id="A1.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the following steps, we will show (<a href="#A1.E15" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: A controllable sequence.<span id="A1.p19.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Fix <math id="A1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By defining a sequence <math id="A1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})\}_{k\geq 0}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})\}_{k\geq 0}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}})={\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}),{\bm{x}}),\quad{\bm{y}}_{0}\textup{ is constant for all }{\bm{x}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is constant for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}})={\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}),{\bm{x}}),\quad{\bm{y}}_{0}\textup{ is constant for all }{\bm{x}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">we are able to estimate the upper bound of <math id="A1.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})\|</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, we decompose <math id="A1.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> by a series:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}=\lim_{k\to\infty}({\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{k})=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}({\bm{y}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k+1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}=\lim_{k\to\infty}({\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{k})=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}({\bm{y}}_{k}-{\bm{y}}_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thanks to (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}})\|\leq\mu_{r}\|{\bm{y}}_{k-1}({\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})\|\cdots\leq\mu_{r}^{k}\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{1}({\bm{x}})\|=\mu_{r}^{k}\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{x}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.1389em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}})\|\leq\mu_{r}\|{\bm{y}}_{k-1}({\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})\|\cdots\leq\mu_{r}^{k}\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{1}({\bm{x}})\|=\mu_{r}^{k}\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{x}})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p19.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.4.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A1.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})\|\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})\|\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})-{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\mu_{r}^{k}\right)\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{x}})\|=\frac{1}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{x}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\mu_{r}^{k}\right)\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{x}})\|=\frac{1}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{x}})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p19.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.5.1" class="ltx_text">Now we can conclude the boundedness of <math id="A1.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})\|</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> by the compactness of <math id="A1.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})\|\leq\underbrace{\|{\bm{y}}_{0}\|+\frac{1}{1-\mu_{r}}\sup_{{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}}\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{x}})\|}_{\textup{defined as $M_{r}\geq 0$.}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>defined as </mtext><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">M</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">≥</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">0</mn></mrow><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})\|\leq\underbrace{\|{\bm{y}}_{0}\|+\frac{1}{1-\mu_{r}}\sup_{{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}}\|{\bm{y}}_{0}-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{0},{\bm{x}})\|}_{\textup{defined as $M_{r}\geq 0$.}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p19.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.6.1" class="ltx_text">With the same argument, we have <math id="A1.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})\|\leq M_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})\|\leq M_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. It implies that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}))\leq L_{1}+L_{2}M_{r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}))\leq L_{1}+L_{2}M_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p19.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.7.1" class="ltx_text">for some <math id="A1.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1},L_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1},L_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> grows linearly w.r.t. <math id="A1.p19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, we can estimate an upper bound for the Lipschitz constant of <math id="A1.p19.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, for <math id="A1.p19.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k+1}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{1})+{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{1})+{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{1})\|+\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{1})\|+\|{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{1})-{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2}),{\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex78.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{r}\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|+(L_{1}+L_{2}M_{r})\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{r}\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|+(L_{1}+L_{2}M_{r})\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p19.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p19.8.1" class="ltx_text">For simplicity, let <math id="A1.p19.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{r}:=L_{1}+L_{2}M_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{r}:=L_{1}+L_{2}M_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p19.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}:=\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}:=\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:=\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:=\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. By recursively applying <math id="A1.p19.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k+1}\leq\mu_{r}a_{k}+Lh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k+1}\leq\mu_{r}a_{k}+Lh</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p19.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|=a_{k}\leq(\mu_{r})^{k}a_{0}+(\mu_{r}^{k-1}+\cdots+\mu_{r}+1)L_{r}h\leq\frac{1}{1-\mu_{r}}L_{r}h=\frac{L_{r}}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|=a_{k}\leq(\mu_{r})^{k}a_{0}+(\mu_{r}^{k-1}+\cdots+\mu_{r}+1)L_{r}h\leq\frac{1}{1-\mu_{r}}L_{r}h=\frac{L_{r}}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4: Final proof.<span id="A1.p20.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
As <math id="A1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is contractive in <math id="A1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A1.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})\to{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}})\to{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{D}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. (Here, as for the “convergence,” we mean the pointwise convergence, which is enough here. We don’t need stronger conditions like the uniform convergence.) For the above <math id="A1.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{1},{\bm{x}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a <math id="A1.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{1})\|\leq\frac{L_{r}}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|,\quad\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq\frac{L_{r}}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{1})\|\leq\frac{L_{r}}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|,\quad\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq\frac{L_{r}}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A1.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq K</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining the above results, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})\|+\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|+\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})\|+\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{1})-{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|+\|{\bm{y}}_{k}({\bm{x}}_{2})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}}_{2})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{3L_{r}}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{3L_{r}}{1-\mu_{r}}\|{\bm{x}}_{1}-{\bm{x}}_{2}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p20.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p20.3.1" class="ltx_text">By letting <math id="A1.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{r}=3L_{r}/(1-\mu_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{r}=3L_{r}/(1-\mu_{r})</annotation></semantics></math>, we get (<a href="#A1.E15" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix A Proofs of main results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Remark: Our result relaxes two uniformity requirements in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, Thm. 1A.4]</cite>: (i) the contraction modulus <math id="A1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is allowed to vary with <math id="A1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> (it only needs to be continuous in <math id="A1.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>), rather than being a single global constant; and (ii) for each <math id="A1.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the mapping <math id="A1.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}},{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz on <math id="A1.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> with a constant that may grow linearly in <math id="A1.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{y}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{y}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, instead of being uniformly bounded in <math id="A1.p21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Because these bounds are not uniform, we conclude only local (as opposed to global) Lipschitz continuity of the fixed-point map <math id="A1.p21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\bm{y}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p21.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>A variant architecture</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, many works use a variant of the vanilla model <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{\ast}={\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{\ast}={\mathcal{G}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{\ast}={\mathcal{G}}({\bm{z}}_{\ast},{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}({\bm{x}})),\quad{\bm{y}}_{\ast}={\mathcal{Q}}_{2}({\bm{z}}_{\ast})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{\ast}={\mathcal{G}}({\bm{z}}_{\ast},{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}({\bm{x}})),\quad{\bm{y}}_{\ast}={\mathcal{Q}}_{2}({\bm{z}}_{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the core implicit model, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a encoding network and <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a decoding (readout).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At inference, one iterates <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{t}={\mathcal{G}}({\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}({\bm{x}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{t}={\mathcal{G}}({\bm{z}}_{t-1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}({\bm{x}}))</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math> and finally <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{T}={\mathcal{Q}}_{2}({\bm{z}}_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{T}={\mathcal{Q}}_{2}({\bm{z}}_{T})</annotation></semantics></math>. This often improves empirical performance but does not alter the expressivity in Theorems <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4 (Sufficiency). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>–<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 2.5 (Necessity). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 2.2. ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> there exists a regular implicit operator <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and globally Lipschitz maps <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}\left(\mathrm{Fix}\big({\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}({\bm{x}}))\big)\right)={\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Fix</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}\left(\mathrm{Fix}\big({\mathcal{G}}(\cdot,{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}({\bm{x}}))\big)\right)={\mathcal{F}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Conversely, for any regular implicit operator <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> any globally Lipschitz <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the fixed point <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by </span>(<a href="#A2.E16" title="In Appendix B A variant architecture ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> exists uniquely and the induced map <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\bm{y}}_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\bm{y}}_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> must be locally Lipschitz on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The claim follows directly from Theorems <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4 (Sufficiency). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>–<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 2.5 (Necessity). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Sufficiency.</em><span id="A2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Given any locally Lipschitz target <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 2.4 (Sufficiency). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a> ensures the existence of a regular <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose fixed-point map equals <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as both identity maps recovers the sufficiency statement with globally Lipschitz <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Necessity.</em><span id="A2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Suppose <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> is regular and <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{1},{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are globally Lipschitz. Then the composite update <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{z}},{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}({\bm{x}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{G}}({\bm{z}},{\mathcal{Q}}_{1}({\bm{x}}))</annotation></semantics></math> is still regular in <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 2.5 (Necessity). ‣ 2. Main Results ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a>, for every <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a unique fixed point <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and the map <math id="A2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\bm{z}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\bm{z}}_{\ast}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz on <math id="A2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, applying the globally Lipschitz readout <math id="A2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{Q}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves local Lipschitz continuity, so <math id="A2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\bm{y}}_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\mapsto{\bm{y}}_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz as claimed.
The proof is finished.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section proves that the target solution mappings, <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{1b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{1b}</annotation></semantics></math>, are single-valued and locally Lipschitz on their domain, as stated in Theorems <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.1. Case Study 1: Image Reconstruction (Inverse problems) ‣ 3. Case Studies ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4. ‣ 3.1. Case Study 1: Image Reconstruction (Inverse problems) ‣ 3. Case Studies ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>. Before the proofs, we first provide some definitions that used in Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1. Case Study 1: Image Reconstruction (Inverse problems) ‣ 3. Case Studies ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given a close subset <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕄</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}\subset{\mathbb{R}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, its <span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">reach</span> <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\tau:=\sup\{r&gt;0:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em">:</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau:=\sup\{r&gt;0:</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\textup{ with dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})&lt;r," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> with dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}\textup{ with dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})&lt;r,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{there exists a unique }{\bm{z}}\in{\mathbb{M}}\textup{ such that }\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{z}}\|=\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>there exists a unique </mtext><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mtext> such that </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mtext>dist</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{there exists a unique }{\bm{z}}\in{\mathbb{M}}\textup{ such that }\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{z}}\|=\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">A set with positive reach is also called a “prox-regular” set in the literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">74</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The bi-Lipschitz condition refers to: for some <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu\leq L&lt;+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu\leq L&lt;+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\|{\bm{y}}_{1}-{\bm{y}}_{2}\|\leq\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{1}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{2}\|\leq L\|{\bm{y}}_{1}-{\bm{y}}_{2}\|\quad\forall{\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{M}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\|{\bm{y}}_{1}-{\bm{y}}_{2}\|\leq\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{1}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{2}\|\leq L\|{\bm{y}}_{1}-{\bm{y}}_{2}\|\quad\forall{\bm{y}}_{1},{\bm{y}}_{2}\in{\mathbb{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">According to the definition, it holds that <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu\leq L\leq\sigma_{\textup{max}}&lt;+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu\leq L\leq\sigma_{\textup{max}}&lt;+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
This condition ensures <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as an injective mapping when restricted to <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is important for the recovery guarantee.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark for Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ 3.1. Case Study 1: Image Reconstruction (Inverse problems) ‣ 3. Case Studies ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</span> The assumption that data (particularly images) lies on a smooth manifold has a long and influential history <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">82</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, and it is still widely used in recent literature. The compactness of the data manifold can be achieved by standard techniques like normalization. In addition, reach is an important concept for manifold to ensure the uniqueness of its projection <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>. The overall assumptions on manifolds, smoothness, compactness and positive reach, is typically used in recent literature regarding image and signal processing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib89" title="" class="ltx_ref">89</a>, <a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">75</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>.
The on-manifold bi-Lipschitz condition does <em id="A3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> require <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> to be globally invertible; it merely rules out ill-posedness <em id="A3.p4.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">restricted to</em> <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is closely related to Johnson–Lindenstrauss (JL)–type embeddings in compressive sensing: e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> shows that random matrices are bi-Lipschitz on low-dimensional manifolds with high probability, and JL-style conditions are widely analyzed and used <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, <a href="#bib.bib93" title="" class="ltx_ref">93</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ 3.1. Case Study 1: Image Reconstruction (Inverse problems) ‣ 3. Case Studies ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For simplicity, we first denote the objective functions in (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1. Case Study 1: Image Reconstruction (Inverse problems) ‣ 3. Case Studies ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) as <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}}):=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}\|^{2}+\frac{\alpha}{2}\textup{dist}^{2}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>dist</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}}):=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}\|^{2}+\frac{\alpha}{2}\textup{dist}^{2}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then we introduce some definitions that will be useful in our proof:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{U}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}}):=\{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}:\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})&lt;r\},\quad\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}}):=\{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}:\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})\leq r\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{U}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}}):=\{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}:\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})&lt;r\},\quad\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}}):=\{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}:\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})\leq r\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Here, <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{U}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{U}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> is an open tubular neighborhood of the manifold <math id="A3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> is its closure. As <math id="A3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, the open set <math id="A3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{U}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{U}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> is named as the </span><span id="A3.p5.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">reach tube</span><span id="A3.p5.3.3" class="ltx_text"> of <math id="A3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="A3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>. As introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, within the reach tube, some nice properties of the distance function and projection mapping can be utilized. For any <math id="A3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> or any <math id="A3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, the projection mapping</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}}):=\argmin_{{\bm{z}}\in{\mathbb{M}}}\|{\bm{z}}-{\bm{y}}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}}):=\argmin_{{\bm{z}}\in{\mathbb{M}}}\|{\bm{z}}-{\bm{y}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">is single valued and well defined, and <math id="A3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})=\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})=\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Existence of minimizers of <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A3.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> As <math id="A3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there must be an underlying <math id="A3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\in{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\in{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> (hence <math id="A3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|=\|{\bm{n}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|=\|{\bm{n}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, it holds that</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}}_{\ast})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|^{2}+\frac{\alpha}{2}\textup{dist}^{2}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},{\mathbb{M}})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}+0=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>dist</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}}_{\ast})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|^{2}+\frac{\alpha}{2}\textup{dist}^{2}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},{\mathbb{M}})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}+0=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">In the other hand, for any point outside the tube: <math id="A3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\not\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\not\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective value is lower bounded by:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}})\geq 0+\frac{\alpha}{2}\textup{dist}^{2}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})&gt;\frac{\alpha}{2}r^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>dist</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}})\geq 0+\frac{\alpha}{2}\textup{dist}^{2}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})&gt;\frac{\alpha}{2}r^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">As long as we have large enough <math id="A3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq\frac{\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}}{r^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq\frac{\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}}{r^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">we can ensure <math id="A3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}})&gt;F_{1a}({\bm{y}}_{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}})&gt;F_{1a}({\bm{y}}_{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\not\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\not\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})=\inf_{{\bm{y}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{n}}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})=\inf_{{\bm{y}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is compact, <math id="A3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> must be compact as well. Consequently, the infimum of <math id="A3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is attainable, which concludes the existence of the minimizer of <math id="A3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="A3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, we have the conclusion: It holds for all <math id="A3.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that, condition (<a href="#A3.E18" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) ensures the existence of <math id="A3.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Bound of minimizers of <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A3.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> For any <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the projection <math id="A3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely defined, hence we have</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex90X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}-{\bm{x}}\Big\|=\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}-{\bm{n}}\Big\|=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒏</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}-{\bm{x}}\Big\|=\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}-{\bm{n}}\Big\|=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})+{\bm{A}}{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}-{\bm{n}}\Big\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒏</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})+{\bm{A}}{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}-{\bm{n}}\Big\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex90Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\Big\|-\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\Big\|-\|{\bm{n}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\Big\|-\Big\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\Big\|-\|{\bm{n}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex90Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu\|{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|-\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\|-\|{\bm{n}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu\|{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|-\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\|-\|{\bm{n}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">According to the conclusion in Step 1, as long as</span></p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq\frac{\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}}{r^{2}}&gt;\frac{\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}}{\tau^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq\frac{\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}}{r^{2}}&gt;\frac{\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}}{\tau^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">it holds that the minimizer <math id="A3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> exists and <math id="A3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{r}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&lt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, which allows us to use the above inequalities at the beginning of Step 2. Now we aim to establish an upper bound for <math id="A3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|</annotation></semantics></math> by contradiction. Suppose</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|&gt;\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})\|+2\|{\bm{n}}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|&gt;\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})\|+2\|{\bm{n}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">we will obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{A}}\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{x}}\|\geq\mu\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|-\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})\|-\|{\bm{n}}\|&gt;\|{\bm{n}}\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒏</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{A}}\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{x}}\|\geq\mu\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|-\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})\|-\|{\bm{n}}\|&gt;\|{\bm{n}}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{A}}\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{x}}\|^{2}+\frac{\alpha}{2}\textup{dist}^{2}(\hat{{\bm{y}}},{\mathbb{M}})&gt;\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}+0=F_{1a}({\bm{y}}_{\ast})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>dist</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})=\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{A}}\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{x}}\|^{2}+\frac{\alpha}{2}\textup{dist}^{2}(\hat{{\bm{y}}},{\mathbb{M}})&gt;\frac{1}{2}\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}+0=F_{1a}({\bm{y}}_{\ast}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">This contradicts with the definition of <math id="A3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math>: the minimizer of function <math id="A3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})\|+2\|{\bm{n}}\|\leq\sigma_{\textup{max}}r+2\|{\bm{n}}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒏</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})\|+2\|{\bm{n}}\|\leq\sigma_{\textup{max}}r+2\|{\bm{n}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">which is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">and implies that</span></p>
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})\|+\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq\left(1+\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}\right)r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})\|+\|{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq\left(1+\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}\right)r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.9.1" class="ltx_text">holds for all <math id="A3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes <math id="A3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Positive definiteness of the Hessian of <math id="A3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A3.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
To prove the uniqueness of the solution, we will establish the strict convexity of the objective function <math id="A3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> within a neighborhood around any point of <math id="A3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. To achieve this, we establish the positive definiteness of the Hessian of <math id="A3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> in this step.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕌</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in{\mathbb{U}}_{\tau}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the projection mapping is single valued and the objective function can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{2}\underbrace{\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}\|^{2}}_{f({\bm{y}})}+\frac{\alpha}{2}\underbrace{\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\|^{2}}_{g({\bm{y}})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}})=\frac{1}{2}\underbrace{\|{\bm{x}}-{\bm{A}}{\bm{y}}\|^{2}}_{f({\bm{y}})}+\frac{\alpha}{2}\underbrace{\|{\bm{y}}-{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\|^{2}}_{g({\bm{y}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The smoothness of <math id="A3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> implies the smoothness of <math id="A3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and of the projection mapping, and hence we can take first and second orders of derivatives on <math id="A3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, Theorem 2]</cite>. Thanks to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, Theorem 4.8]</cite>, the gradient and Hessian of <math id="A3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> are given by</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla g({\bm{y}})=2\left({\bm{y}}-{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right),\quad\nabla^{2}g({\bm{y}})=2\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla g({\bm{y}})=2\left({\bm{y}}-{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right),\quad\nabla^{2}g({\bm{y}})=2\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D{\bm{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D{\bm{p}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Jacobian of the projection mapping. The overall Hessian of <math id="A3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math> is provided by</span></p>
<table id="A3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})={\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}+\alpha\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})={\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}+\alpha\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">To further present the properties of the above Hessian, we introduce a space decomposition according to <math id="A3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}^{n}={\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})\oplus{\mathbb{N}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕋</mi><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}^{n}={\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})\oplus{\mathbb{N}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕋</mi><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the tangent space of <math id="A3.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> at the point <math id="A3.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\in{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\in{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{N}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{N}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the normal space. According to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>, Theorem C and Definition 7]</cite>, the matrix <math id="A3.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> is actually restricted to the tangent space. In other words, for any decomposition <math id="A3.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}={\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}+{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}={\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}+{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\in{\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕋</mi><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\in{\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\in{\mathbb{N}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\in{\mathbb{N}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}={\bm{0}},\quad D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\in{\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕋</mi><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}={\bm{0}},\quad D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\in{\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.6.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, function <math id="A3.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.p9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\frac{s}{\tau-s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\frac{s}{\tau-s})</annotation></semantics></math>-weakly convex where <math id="A3.p9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the reach of <math id="A3.p9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\textup{dist}({\bm{y}},{\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>, Section 5]</cite>, and hence the spectrum of <math id="A3.p9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}g</annotation></semantics></math> can be lower bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A3.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},\nabla^{2}g({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\rangle\geq-\frac{2s}{\tau-s}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},\nabla^{2}g({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\rangle\geq-\frac{2s}{\tau-s}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.7.1" class="ltx_text">Now, let’s turn to the first term in the Hessian: <math id="A3.p9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>. It can be shown using the JL condition (<a href="#A3.E17" title="In Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) that, the spectrum of <math id="A3.p9.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> restricted to the tangent space can also be lower bounded. In particular, we pick an arbitrary tangent vector <math id="A3.p9.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\in{\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕋</mi><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\in{\mathbb{T}}_{{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>. According to the definition of tangent space, there must be a curve <math id="A3.p9.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma:(-\delta,\delta)\to{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma:(-\delta,\delta)\to{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.p9.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p9.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(0)={\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(0)={\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p9.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\prime}(0)={\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\prime}(0)={\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A3.p9.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq t&lt;\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq t&lt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p9.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)\in{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕄</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)\in{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By applying condition (<a href="#A3.E17" title="In Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) with the pair <math id="A3.p9.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma(t),\gamma(0))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma(t),\gamma(0))</annotation></semantics></math> and divide by <math id="A3.p9.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{2}\frac{\|\gamma(t)-\gamma(0)\|^{2}}{t^{2}}\leq\frac{\|{\bm{A}}\gamma(t)-{\bm{A}}\gamma(0)\|^{2}}{t^{2}}\leq L^{2}\frac{\|\gamma(t)-\gamma(0)\|^{2}}{t^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{2}\frac{\|\gamma(t)-\gamma(0)\|^{2}}{t^{2}}\leq\frac{\|{\bm{A}}\gamma(t)-{\bm{A}}\gamma(0)\|^{2}}{t^{2}}\leq L^{2}\frac{\|\gamma(t)-\gamma(0)\|^{2}}{t^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.8.1" class="ltx_text">By differentiability and the continuity of the operator <math id="A3.p9.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to 0}\frac{\gamma(t)-\gamma(0)}{t}={\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},\quad\lim_{t\to 0}\frac{{\bm{A}}\gamma(t)-{\bm{A}}\gamma(0)}{t}={\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to 0}\frac{\gamma(t)-\gamma(0)}{t}={\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},\quad\lim_{t\to 0}\frac{{\bm{A}}\gamma(t)-{\bm{A}}\gamma(0)}{t}={\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.9.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A3.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{2}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}\leq\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}\leq L^{2}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{2}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}\leq\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}\leq L^{2}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.10.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A3.E21" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.E22" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.E23" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), and (<a href="#A3.E24" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle{\bm{h}},\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle{\bm{h}},\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex102.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\rangle}_{\geq\mu^{2}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}}+2\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle+\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}},{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\rangle}_{\geq\mu^{2}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}}+2\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle+\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}},{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\alpha\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\rangle}_{\geq-\frac{s}{\tau-s}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}}+2\alpha\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle}_{=\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle=0}+\alpha\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}},\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle}_{=\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒑</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\alpha\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\rangle}_{\geq-\frac{s}{\tau-s}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}}+2\alpha\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle}_{=\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}},{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle=0}+\alpha\underbrace{\langle{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}},\left({\bm{I}}-D{\bm{p}}({\bm{y}})\right){\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\rangle}_{=\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex104.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}\right)\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}+\alpha\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|^{2}-2\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|\cdot\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}\right)\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}+\alpha\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|^{2}-2\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|\cdot\|{\bm{A}}{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex105.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}\right)\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}+\alpha\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|^{2}-2L\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|\cdot\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}\right)\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|^{2}+\alpha\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|^{2}-2L\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|\cdot\sigma_{\textup{max}}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex106.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|&amp;\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}&amp;-\sigma_{\textup{max}}L\\
-\sigma_{\textup{max}}L&amp;\alpha\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|\\
\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi>α</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|&amp;\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}&amp;-\sigma_{\textup{max}}L\\
-\sigma_{\textup{max}}L&amp;\alpha\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{T}}\|\\
\|{\bm{h}}_{\mathrm{N}}\|\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.11.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, to ensure <math id="A3.p9.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\bm{h}},\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}\rangle&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\bm{h}},\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}}){\bm{h}}\rangle&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A3.p9.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}\neq{\bm{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}\neq{\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it’s enough to ensure the <math id="A3.p9.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> matrix to be positive definite:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}&gt;0\quad\textup{and}\quad\alpha\left(\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}\right)-\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}&gt;0\quad\textup{and}\quad\alpha\left(\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}\right)-\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.12.1" class="ltx_text">In other words, (<a href="#A3.E25" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) will guarantee the positive definiteness of <math id="A3.p9.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.p9.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{s}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{s}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A3.p9.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s&lt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4: Uniqueness of minimizers of <math id="A3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A3.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> In this step, we will combine the results from Steps 2 and 3. Then we are able to prove that the objective function <math id="A3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly convex in a neighborhood of its minimizers, which implies the uniqueness of the minimizer. To achieve this, it’s enough to ensure</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq s" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{y}}_{\ast}\|\leq s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in\argmin_{{\bm{y}}}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mi>𝐲</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in\argmin_{{\bm{y}}}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies (<a href="#A3.E25" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>). With this condition (<a href="#A3.E26" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>), it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},s)\subset\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{s}({\mathbb{M}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}\in{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},s)\subset\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{s}({\mathbb{M}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Along with the fact that <math id="A3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},s)</annotation></semantics></math> is convex and that <math id="A3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}F_{1a}({\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite for all <math id="A3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{s}({\mathbb{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝕌</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝕄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}\in\overline{{\mathbb{U}}}_{s}({\mathbb{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly convex within <math id="A3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},s)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, Section 3.1.4]</cite>. As all minimizers of the strict convex function belong to this convex set, <math id="A3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔹</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{B}}({\bm{y}}_{\ast},s)</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimizer <math id="A3.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> must be unique.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now the question is: How to guarantee (<a href="#A3.E26" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>)? According to (<a href="#A3.E20" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), Condition (<a href="#A3.E19" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) along with</span></p>
<table id="A3.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(1+\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}\right)r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|\leq s" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(1+\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}\right)r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|\leq s</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">can guarantee (<a href="#A3.E26" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>). Finally, it’s enough to choose <math id="A3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> such that (<a href="#A3.E19" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.E25" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), and (<a href="#A3.E27" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) are satisfied together. In particular, we choose</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\frac{4}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|,\quad r=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}\|{\bm{n}}\|,\quad\alpha=\frac{2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}{\mu^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\frac{4}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|,\quad r=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}\|{\bm{n}}\|,\quad\alpha=\frac{2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}{\mu^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> merely depends on <math id="A3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> but is independent of <math id="A3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Such a parameter choice implies (<a href="#A3.E27" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(1+\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}\right)r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|\leq 2\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|=\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|=s." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒏</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(1+\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}\right)r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|\leq 2\frac{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}{\mu}r+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|=\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|+\frac{2}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|=s.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{n}}\|&lt;\frac{1}{20}\frac{\mu^{5}}{\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{n}}\|&lt;\frac{1}{20}\frac{\mu^{5}}{\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\frac{4}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|&lt;\frac{\mu^{4}}{5\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau~~\implies~~\frac{s}{\tau-s}&lt;\frac{\frac{\mu^{4}}{5\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau}{\tau-\frac{\mu^{4}}{5\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau}\leq\frac{\frac{\mu^{4}}{5\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau}{\tau-\frac{1}{5}\tau}=\frac{\mu^{4}}{4\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.938em" rspace="0.938em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\frac{4}{\mu}\|{\bm{n}}\|&lt;\frac{\mu^{4}}{5\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau~~\implies~~\frac{s}{\tau-s}&lt;\frac{\frac{\mu^{4}}{5\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau}{\tau-\frac{\mu^{4}}{5\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau}\leq\frac{\frac{\mu^{4}}{5\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau}{\tau-\frac{1}{5}\tau}=\frac{\mu^{4}}{4\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore (<a href="#A3.E25" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) is satisfied:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}&gt;\mu^{2}-\frac{2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\frac{\mu^{4}}{4\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}=\frac{1}{2}\mu^{2}&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}&gt;\mu^{2}-\frac{2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\frac{\mu^{4}}{4\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}=\frac{1}{2}\mu^{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.6.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\left(\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}\right)&gt;\frac{2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\mu^{2}=\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\left(\mu^{2}-\alpha\frac{s}{\tau-s}\right)&gt;\frac{2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\mu^{2}=\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.7.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, by choosing <math id="A3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> as before, condition (<a href="#A3.E19" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proofs of Theorems for Inverse Problems ‣ Implicit Models: Expressive Power Scales with Test-Time Compute" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) is satisfied:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}\cdot\frac{L^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\geq 2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}=\frac{2\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}}{r^{2}},\quad r=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}\|{\bm{n}}\|&lt;\frac{1}{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}\cdot\frac{1}{20}\frac{\mu^{5}}{\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau&lt;\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒏</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mtext>max</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}\cdot\frac{L^{2}}{\mu^{2}}\geq 2\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}=\frac{2\|{\bm{n}}\|^{2}}{r^{2}},\quad r=\frac{1}{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}\|{\bm{n}}\|&lt;\frac{1}{\sigma_{\textup{max}}}\cdot\frac{1}{20}\frac{\mu^{5}}{\sigma^{2}_{\textup{max}}L^{2}}\tau&lt;\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.8.1" class="ltx_text">which finishes the proof of the uniqueness of minimizers of <math id="A3.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 5: Local Lipschitz continuity of <math id="A3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{F}}_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{F}}_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A3.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Previous results from Steps 1-4 indicate that, for any <math id="A3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a unique <math id="A3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes <math id="A3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>, but the continuity of <math id="A3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> has not been established. In this step, we will show this continuity via the implicit function theorem.
Firstly, as <math id="A3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math> minimizes <math id="A3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1a}</annotation></semantics></math>, by first-order optimality conditions for smooth minimization, it holds that</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla F_{1a}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})=\underbrace{{\bm{A}}^{\top}({\bm{A}}\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{x}})+\alpha(\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}}))}_{=:{\mathcal{H}}({\bm{x}},\hat{{\bm{y}}})}={\bm{0}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla F_{1a}(\hat{{\bm{y}}})=\underbrace{{\bm{A}}^{\top}({\bm{A}}\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{x}})+\alpha(\hat{{\bm{y}}}-{\bm{p}}(\hat{{\bm{y}}}))}_{=:{\mathcal{H}}({\bm{x}},\hat{{\bm{y}}})}={\bm{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now, let’s pick a point <math id="A3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A3.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝕏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Previous results from Steps 1-4 indicate that, operator <math id="A3.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{H}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{H}}({\bm{x}},{\bm{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> is continuously differentiable within a neighborhood of <math id="A3.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{x}}_{0},\hat{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{x}}_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{x}}_{0},\hat{{\bm{y}}}({\bm{x}}_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math>, and its Jacobian matrix w.r.t. <math id="A3.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<tabl